# Deliberately empty of `parameters:` — silver-assist-security (the one
# real precedent in the org for a plugin composing PHPStan config across
# SilverAssist packages) doesn't use `scanDirectories: [vendor]` either;
# it lists precise `stubFiles`
# instead (e.g. vendor/axepress/wp-graphql-stubs/wp-graphql-stubs.php).
# `scanDirectories` also has the exact same relative-path resolution bug
# as `includes:` below — found the same way, by actually running
# `vendor/bin/phpstan` against wp-plugin-kernel and hitting "Scanned
# directory .../phpstan/vendor does not exist". A consuming plugin that
# needs extra stub files should list them explicitly in its own
# `phpstan.neon`, the same way silver-assist-security does.
#
# Deliberately does NOT `includes:` silverassist/coding-standards' base.neon
# or szepeviktor/phpstan-wordpress's extension.neon from here, even though
# conceptually this file "composes" both. PHPStan resolves relative
# `includes:` paths relative to THIS file's own location on disk — which
# works when this package is the project root (e.g. running `composer
# test` inside wp-coding-standards itself) but breaks once this file is
# consumed as a dependency: Composer flattens `silverassist/coding-standards`
# and `szepeviktor/phpstan-wordpress` into the *consumer's* top-level
# vendor/, not into a nested vendor/ inside this package (which doesn't
# get its own `composer install` run at all in that scenario). A relative
# `../vendor/...` path from here then points at a directory that doesn't
# exist. Found by actually running `vendor/bin/phpstan` against a real
# dependent package (wp-plugin-kernel).
#
# Consumers must `includes:` all three files directly, from their own
# phpstan.neon (all relative to their own root, which is unambiguous):
#
#   includes:
#       - vendor/silverassist/coding-standards/phpstan/base.neon
#       - vendor/silverassist/wp-coding-standards/phpstan/base.neon
#       - vendor/szepeviktor/phpstan-wordpress/extension.neon
#
# See this package's README for the full consumer snippet.
